WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
In Turkey, a reed flute
called the ney begins to play.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.430
Figures in tall felt hats and
white robes start to turn:

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.140
right palm up, left palm down.

4
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:15.970
For these Sufis, the music and the
turning are a way of remembering Allah.

5
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.370
But many other Muslims say
musical instruments are forbidden,

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.270
and dancing has no place in worship.

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.140
So why do Muslims disagree so
sharply about music and dance?

8
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.680
In this mission, you'll hear
Sufi devotion in action:

9
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.800
whirling, qawwali songs and poetry.

10
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.720
Then you'll read two short
reports about the Prophet,

11
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.120
and weigh up music in worship.

12
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:44.110
Your mission: find out why Muslims disagree
about music and dance in remembering

13
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:44.750
Allah.
